<!-- Conclusion -->
<section id="sec-conclusion" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>Use the Secant Ratio With Confidence</h2>
  <p>Secant is the flipped form of cosine: divide the hypotenuse by the adjacent side and you have described how much longer the sloping length is than its horizontal footprint. The formula <span set:html={rich('[[\\sec(A)=c/b]]')} /> needs only two measurements, the answer is always a dimensionless number greater than 1, and it grows as the reference angle grows. When a missing side is needed, <span set:html={rich('[[c=b\\sec(A)]]')} /> recovers the hypotenuse; when the angle is needed, <span set:html={rich('[[A=\\cos^{-1}(1/\\sec(A))]]')} /> recovers it. Ladder, rafter, ramp, or textbook 3-4-5, the method never changes: identify the hypotenuse, identify the adjacent side, divide, and verify with the reciprocal of cosine.</p>
</section>
